# Copy to .env.local for local development.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Cognito Hosted UI — this app redirects the browser here to sign in (there is no
# email/password form of its own; Cognito's own hosted page collects the credential
# and, per apps/api's own COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID/COGNITO_CLIENT_ID comment, MFA is
# Required at the Pool's own configuration). Real AWS infrastructure this codebase
# cannot provision — see apps/api/.env.example's own comment on the same point.
# Leave unset for local development without a real Cognito Pool: the login screen
# degrades to a clear "not configured" message instead of a broken redirect.
#
# VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN is the Pool's own Hosted UI domain, e.g.
# "https://ultm8-platform-admin.auth.us-east-1.amazoncognito.com" (no trailing slash).
# VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID must be an App Client on that same Pool configured for the
# Authorization Code grant with PKCE (response_type=code) — the same flow apps/api's
# own PlatformAdminAuthController/CognitoTokenVerifierService already document as
# what they expect. No client secret: PKCE is exactly the mechanism that lets a
# public client (this browser SPA) use the Authorization Code flow safely, so the
# App Client must be created WITHOUT a client secret (or with "Generate client
# secret" left unchecked) — see src/auth/pkce.ts for the full reasoning.
VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=
# Must be registered as an exact Callback URL on that same App Client.
VITE_COGNITO_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5174/login
